{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>With their wiles by which they dealt wily with you.</b> Through stratagems and evil counsels with which they schemed against you. And this indicates that the elders of Midian devised the evil plan and gave counsel to Moab to cause their daughters to sin with the people of Israel, in order to entice them and cleave them to Baal Peor." "<b>And concerning the matter of Cozbi the daughter of a prince of Midian.</b> He could have said 'daughter of Zur,' as he said above, כזבי בת צור, but he mentioned Midian to show that this was the counsel of the elders of Midian — to send the king's daughter to commit harlotry with them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:09.835548956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}